Aside from what has been said by others in this thread:

On Oct 25, 6:07=A0pm, Martin <Mar...@mail.invalid> wrote:
> koloa the Woman-at-arms   St:6 Dx:14 Co:17 In:5 Wi:9 Ch:8  Lawful

Strength 6? What happened? A unicorn horn is a high-priority item. By
XL 10 / DL 14 you should have come across at least one unicorn; have
your pet kill it (there are disadvantages to doing so yourself, some
very major if you kill the wrong kind, but not the least that they can
do a lot of damage).

> Dlvl:14 $:5698 HP:92(92) Pw:13(13) AC:10 Exp:10 Burdened

You're carrying a lot of money. Money isn't very useful to carry
around deeper in the dungeon unless you are lucky enough to find deep-
level shops; if you're having weight-management problems, either find
a priest to donate to or stash it. And when beseiged by monsters, big
heavy stacks of cash that are slowing you down are an *excellent*
thing to drop! You can always come get it later when you've cleared
out the nasties.

Why AC 10? That's worse than you start off with! Sorting through armor
left by monsters to get your AC down is another high priority.

> All my scrolls were burnt by some monster.

Anything in open inventory is at risk. If you can't find a bag, carry
only the most immediately useful stuff and stash the rest when
exploring.

> I lost my weapons and am fighting barehands now.

How did you loose your weapons? Why haven't you been able to find
anything to replace them with? Not even a dagger scavenged off an orc?

> I've been trapped in a corridor surrounded by winter wolves from both
> sides.
> - I engraved Elbereth - it says that a wolf pulls back, but then it
> =A0 starts biting me again.

The "pulled back" message is for monsters who try to attack during
prayer; perhaps you have them confused. Engraving has a chance of
failure; use the "look" command (:) to check that the engraving is
correct. Also, even if it is correct, dust-Elbereth smudges easily and
will need to be re-engraved frequently, and in any case it won't
prevent monsters from using ranged attacks (although, as a Valk, you
should be immune to the winter wolves' cold attack).

> - I prayed - the god was pleased but it doesn't change anything

Prayer will only cure low hit-points and other issues with your
condition. It won't do anything about monsters attacking you, aside
from the duration of the prayer itself.

> - I tried to apply (break a wand of light) - it says I don't have enough
> =A0 strength.

Breaking a wand of light just lights the place up. Not more helpful
than just zapping it.

> =A0 Barehands I don't do much damage but sometimes I a wolf gets killed
> =A0 from my blows.

Your big problem here is strength 6, which is very, very weak.
Barehands attacks would do a lot more damage at higher strength.

> More often, they die from each other winter blasts.

Hmm? Winter wolves should be immune to cold. Perhaps there are some
normal wolves mixed in?

>  I can't see an end to them. Is this the end?

It sounds like there might be a werewolf nearby creating wolves by
"summoning their brethren". Otherwise there should be at most about
4-6 wolves or winter wolves created at a time.

Under normal conditions I'd suggest using Elbereth (checking that it's
written correctly) to keep them away from you (as you should be immune
to their breath attack), and slowly working your way to a corridor,
where there can be at most two monsters next to you at any time (move
one square, engrave Elbereth, check that it's correct and re-engrave
if necessary, wait for all the monsters to be scared away, move one
square, repeat). Then once you're in a corridor, try to block the
wolves out (close the door if there is one at either end), run for the
stairs (the upstairs if possible), and regroup. If you're already in a
corridor, engrave Elbereth a bunch of times (but only one engraving at
a time), making sure that at least 3-4 of them are correct, drop
something (like that empty wand of digging), wait until the square
next to you on the side you want to travel to (i.e., the side near the
stairs) is clear, move onto it, and then start the Elbereth-scare-move-
Elbereth cycle until you get to the stairs.

If there is indeed a werewolf around... well, in your condition
getting bitten and becoming a werewolf might have short-term
advantages, in that it would be easy to generate decent pets (and then
go find a unicorn and have them kill it, hint hint). Lycanthropy is
kind of a pain, and curing it is not that easy, but with no armor and
no weapons you're not doing so well as it is.

Also, the "." direction for zapping translates as "at myself". Wands
of digging have no effects on monsters (such as yourself), as you have
discovered. To zap downwards, use ">".

Playing in Explore mode was quite useful to me at first, to get a feel
for the monsters, the items, the structure of the dungeon and possible
tactics. But it has the unfortunate effect of encouraging careless
play, and in this case I think something very bad happened to you that
you may not have understood / appreciated. Try to think about how you
got to strength 6, and how you lost your weapons / armor, and how you
can avoid having whatever it was happen again :)


